WEBVTT

00:36.619 --> 00:38.121
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO
Push Start!

00:38.955 --> 00:40.165
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

01:33.593 --> 01:36.554
What? It floats into the sky
and shoots out light?

01:37.389 --> 01:39.015
What kind of face does it have?

01:39.599 --> 01:42.811
Don't ask me everything.
Imagine for yourself, Kona.

01:43.561 --> 01:44.771
Close your eyes,

01:44.854 --> 01:47.357
and focus on what comes to mind.
Look at it closely.

01:49.693 --> 01:52.654
It might be something you think
you saw out of the corner of your eye,

01:52.737 --> 01:54.781
or an optical illusion.

01:54.864 --> 01:56.491
But let it fill your senses. Follow it.

02:03.373 --> 02:04.416
Did you see something?

02:05.375 --> 02:07.252
A sword of light?

02:09.462 --> 02:11.214
-Michika?
-Blood.

02:12.799 --> 02:14.300
What's happened?

02:14.384 --> 02:16.886
-Michika suddenly started bleeding.
-Get the teacher!

02:16.970 --> 02:18.596
It's a deep cut.

02:19.097 --> 02:21.891
No one even touched Michika.
It came out of nowhere.

02:22.892 --> 02:25.311
Michika, please stay still.

02:32.444 --> 02:35.155
It's not perfect, so please rest, okay?

02:48.168 --> 02:50.211
Kona? Kona.

02:52.881 --> 02:54.716
What? Asura?

02:56.092 --> 02:57.844
When did you come in?

03:01.139 --> 03:03.767
-Oh, no!
-A power outage?

03:04.267 --> 03:06.936
No, wait. It's just the camera monitors.

03:07.520 --> 03:08.396
Restart them!

03:08.480 --> 03:10.523
CAMERAS ARE NOT RESPONDING

03:10.607 --> 03:14.778
Now I understand why I was born.

03:15.528 --> 03:17.655
So I have come to say goodbye.

03:17.739 --> 03:18.823
What?

03:20.033 --> 03:21.076
Asura?

03:21.159 --> 03:22.160
Asura!

03:23.453 --> 03:24.913
Asura, where are you?

03:24.996 --> 03:26.581
Asura.

03:56.903 --> 03:58.947
Asura!

04:13.211 --> 04:14.963
<i>The adults are on their way.</i>

04:15.505 --> 04:17.382
<i>Go back to your room, Kona.</i>

04:17.465 --> 04:19.634
Asura, don't go!

04:20.510 --> 04:22.137
I'll be all alone!

04:23.179 --> 04:24.556
<i>You are not alone.</i>

04:25.682 --> 04:29.019
<i>You have Anzu, Tokio and Mimihime.</i>

04:29.686 --> 04:31.604
<i>Even Nanaki, Iwa and the others.</i>

04:32.147 --> 04:33.815
<i>You will find more and more friends.</i>

04:34.774 --> 04:37.193
<i>Kona, find someone that you love.</i>

04:37.694 --> 04:39.446
But I love you, Asura!

04:40.155 --> 04:43.616
<i>It's a different kind of love.</i>
<i>An even more special feeling.</i>

04:45.368 --> 04:46.494
<i>Open your heart to it.</i>

04:55.795 --> 04:58.048
Kona seems lonely.

04:58.548 --> 05:01.968
Kona is the only one left in his year now.

05:03.553 --> 05:04.679
I'll be right back.

05:05.263 --> 05:06.348
Tokio!

05:15.023 --> 05:16.691
What is it, Tokio?

05:16.775 --> 05:19.444
It's nothing important…

05:21.237 --> 05:24.032
but I just thought I'd come over here.

05:26.576 --> 05:28.161
You're so good at drawing.

05:35.293 --> 05:36.336
Thank you.

05:50.016 --> 05:51.935
Whoever killed Asura,

05:52.894 --> 05:54.604
is coming to take Tokio away next.

05:54.688 --> 05:57.107
CHILDREN OF THE NURSERY

06:05.407 --> 06:07.283
That was so close.

06:08.076 --> 06:11.413
They are the group of 14-year-olds.

06:11.496 --> 06:12.664
That's great.

06:16.209 --> 06:17.836
<i>Tokio? Could it be?</i>

06:18.503 --> 06:22.424
And a group of 15 five-year-olds
will join the nursery.

06:22.507 --> 06:24.926
They will probably be the last.

06:26.469 --> 06:29.305
Oh, Miss Aoshima, what are you doing?

06:29.389 --> 06:30.640
I need you to interpret.

06:31.182 --> 06:32.308
Sorry.

06:34.394 --> 06:38.523
Usami was holding this button.
It has the same logo as Kiru-Beam.

06:39.024 --> 06:41.526
It can't just be a coincidence.

06:42.694 --> 06:45.572
<i>Since you only have a vague idea</i>
<i>of where you're trying to go,</i>

06:45.655 --> 06:47.949
<i>I think tracking down this logo</i>
<i>is a good idea.</i>

06:49.034 --> 06:51.411
So the next place we need to go is--

06:52.078 --> 06:54.122
The town where Usami used to live?

06:54.205 --> 06:55.457
That's the one.

06:55.540 --> 06:58.543
I thought we'd be going that way
with Usami,

06:58.626 --> 07:01.129
so I didn't see
where he pointed on the map.

07:01.713 --> 07:04.632
Everyone else went off that way.

07:04.716 --> 07:07.719
Yeah, but if they turned off
here or there…

07:08.428 --> 07:11.723
If they did that,
then there are endless possibilities.

07:11.806 --> 07:14.476
Don't make it sound like a good thing.

07:14.559 --> 07:17.228
Well, either way,
we've just got to try to get there.

07:17.312 --> 07:19.856
Oh, and by the way, look.

07:20.899 --> 07:22.984
The tooth that fell out.
It's growing back.

07:23.068 --> 07:25.570
What's going on with your body?

07:31.159 --> 07:32.994
-An earthquake.
-It's a big one.

07:34.037 --> 07:35.163
Whoa!

07:35.246 --> 07:37.749
Careful! If the ground swallows you up,
you're done for.

07:45.298 --> 07:47.092
There hasn't been an earthquake in ages.

07:49.094 --> 07:51.346
That must be a building falling nearby.

07:51.429 --> 07:52.972
-Let's go.
-What for?

07:53.556 --> 07:55.433
When a building falls down,

07:55.517 --> 07:57.936
you can get into any room.
It's a total jackpot.

07:58.019 --> 08:01.731
If it's near the town we're looking for,
resource collectors might show up.

08:02.315 --> 08:04.984
You wanna grab anything worth stealing
before those guys?

08:05.068 --> 08:07.821
You idiot. They can take us
to the place we're looking for.

08:13.618 --> 08:15.870
It didn't collapse completely.
It'll be dangerous.

08:19.082 --> 08:20.667
We can get in this way.

08:20.750 --> 08:22.836
Give it up. If it caves in, we'll die.

08:27.674 --> 08:30.010
What the hell? Someone's living in there!

08:30.510 --> 08:32.053
Oh, wow, are you okay?

08:32.637 --> 08:34.180
You did well to survive.

08:34.264 --> 08:37.183
No, no. I don't live there.

08:37.267 --> 08:39.811
I came to have a look
to see if there are any resources.

08:39.894 --> 08:41.855
Looks like you beat us to it.

08:41.938 --> 08:42.981
Sorry.

08:43.064 --> 08:48.028
I couldn't get in at all,
and I don't have anything either.

08:48.111 --> 08:49.779
Can you let it slide?

08:49.863 --> 08:51.573
What are you so nervous for?

08:52.157 --> 08:54.993
Well, from the look of you,
aren't you guys bandits?

08:57.078 --> 08:58.705
Who you calling bandits?

08:58.788 --> 09:01.124
You stink of bandits way more than us!

09:01.207 --> 09:02.250
I-I'm sorr…

09:02.834 --> 09:04.586
I'm sorry for taking up your time.

09:05.170 --> 09:07.255
Please excuse me
for calling you here so suddenly.

09:07.339 --> 09:11.134
It's okay. I've been anxious
about my health recently too.

09:11.217 --> 09:12.719
Thank you for checking up on me.

09:13.428 --> 09:16.264
Everything seems perfectly okay,
so no need to worry.

09:16.806 --> 09:19.309
For now, just try not to catch a chill.

09:20.060 --> 09:21.603
And don't do any strenuous activity.

09:23.229 --> 09:25.106
Okay. I won't.

09:29.027 --> 09:30.153
Mimihime.

09:30.904 --> 09:32.322
You made me jump.

09:32.405 --> 09:34.157
Don't sneak up on me like that.

09:35.075 --> 09:38.286
You're always
looking at something up there.

09:38.370 --> 09:40.622
And you're always looking at me.

09:44.584 --> 09:45.960
Is it the ceiling?

09:46.044 --> 09:48.630
It's something floating
in front of the ceiling.

09:49.339 --> 09:50.340
Dust?

09:50.840 --> 09:53.051
If you're talking about
specks of light floating about,

09:53.134 --> 09:55.136
they're particles
in your eyes' vitreous fluid.

09:56.221 --> 09:58.556
Anyway, let's go. Class is about to start.

10:02.060 --> 10:03.061
I see.

10:03.770 --> 10:04.771
Just as I thought.

10:05.855 --> 10:07.982
I'm the only one who can see it.

10:10.110 --> 10:11.111
It's creepy.

10:11.194 --> 10:13.738
Really? Can no one else see that?

10:16.449 --> 10:18.034
<i>Is everyone present?</i>

10:18.660 --> 10:19.953
Tokio isn't here yet.

10:21.121 --> 10:22.539
<i>Before class begins,</i>

10:22.622 --> 10:25.208
<i>I need to inform you</i>
<i>of something about Tokio.</i>

10:26.292 --> 10:29.629
-<i>You may not see Tokio for some time.</i>
-What?

10:31.047 --> 10:33.299
<i>But, of course, you will meet again.</i>

10:35.218 --> 10:36.803
<i>Please don't worry.</i>

10:40.473 --> 10:42.017
<i>Let's begin the class.</i>

10:44.394 --> 10:45.311
There.

10:48.982 --> 10:51.484
Must be nice to have a car that works.

10:51.985 --> 10:55.739
It's not as useful as you might think,
when the roads are such a mess.

10:56.448 --> 10:57.699
Well, I'm all set then.

10:58.283 --> 10:59.534
Isn't it dangerous by yourself?

11:03.788 --> 11:05.623
Worst-case scenario, I've got this.

11:06.583 --> 11:09.377
You had something that dangerous
hidden under your raincoat?

11:10.086 --> 11:11.796
Well, isn't that a gun?

11:11.880 --> 11:12.881
Something like that.

11:13.465 --> 11:15.925
Hey, is there a town somewhere round here?

11:16.009 --> 11:19.012
Information is a commodity, you know.

11:19.095 --> 11:21.056
If it's money you want, we'll pay.

11:21.139 --> 11:23.850
In any case,
do either of these guys, this logo,

11:24.517 --> 11:28.021
or the word "heaven" mean anything to you?

11:31.524 --> 11:33.109
Wait there a minute.

11:34.903 --> 11:37.072
I just need to move the car a bit.
Can you step back?

11:41.409 --> 11:43.870
A bit further! A bit more!

11:53.296 --> 11:56.174
There. Now we can talk properly.

11:56.257 --> 12:01.137
I get the feeling
I might know where that logo comes from.

12:01.221 --> 12:02.597
Oh, really?

12:02.681 --> 12:05.141
I'll tell you in exchange for the gun.

12:05.225 --> 12:06.685
It's not for sale.

12:06.768 --> 12:08.436
In that case, money will do.

12:08.520 --> 12:10.146
That was easy.

12:10.230 --> 12:13.149
Well, there's no point complaining
and getting myself killed.

12:13.983 --> 12:18.029
But it may
take me a little while to remember.

12:18.780 --> 12:22.617
I make a living
selling the information I have.

12:22.701 --> 12:25.286
I'm sure once I get talking
it'll jog my memory.

12:25.370 --> 12:27.622
This guy is really milking it.

12:28.206 --> 12:30.125
Just tell us
whichever one you think is best.

12:33.003 --> 12:34.838
Good evening, everyone.

12:35.338 --> 12:37.257
I have returned once more.

12:37.757 --> 12:40.260
I, Juichi, am here to tell you

12:40.760 --> 12:42.929
stories that may have really happened.

12:43.513 --> 12:44.848
It's still daytime.

12:46.349 --> 12:49.102
There are various rumors
about what caused the Great Disaster.

12:49.185 --> 12:51.855
But why does the cause remain so unclear?

12:51.938 --> 12:54.983
Because the subsequent earthquakes,
the abnormally long winters,

12:55.066 --> 12:58.153
the famine and disease, led humanity
towards the edge of extinction,

12:58.236 --> 13:01.448
<i>making it impossible to trace back</i>
<i>to what originally happened.</i>

13:01.531 --> 13:03.366
<i>These three theories persist.</i>

13:03.450 --> 13:05.201
1 ASTEROID IMPACT
2 ALIEN INVASION - 3 WAR THEORY

13:05.285 --> 13:07.704
<i>First is the asteroid impact theory.</i>

13:07.787 --> 13:11.791
<i>Before the Great Disaster,</i>
<i>people were making a lot of noise</i>

13:11.875 --> 13:14.294
<i>about the discovery</i>
<i>of an asteroid drawing closer to Earth.</i>

13:14.794 --> 13:17.297
<i>The sheer scale of the disaster</i>
<i>makes this theory a strong one.</i>

13:18.298 --> 13:20.550
Next, the alien invasion theory.

13:20.633 --> 13:24.804
It may seem absurd at first,
but some people think

13:24.888 --> 13:28.475
that those man-eating life-forms
came to Earth from space.

13:29.059 --> 13:30.685
<i>Before the Great Disaster occurred,</i>

13:30.769 --> 13:34.564
<i>many people witnessed</i>
<i>mysterious figures floating in the sky.</i>

13:35.065 --> 13:38.693
I managed to get hold
of this precious image from back then.

13:38.777 --> 13:39.861
That's a bird.

13:39.944 --> 13:42.238
Finally, the war theory.

13:42.322 --> 13:44.199
<i>There is a rumor</i>
<i>that before the Great Disaster,</i>

13:44.282 --> 13:47.452
<i>there was a terrorist attack</i>
<i>somewhere in Japan.</i>

13:47.535 --> 13:50.163
<i>The theory goes that</i>
<i>this caused an outbreak of war</i>

13:50.246 --> 13:53.583
<i>and the use</i>
<i>of some sort of special weapon.</i>

13:54.793 --> 13:56.711
So, how was the story?

13:56.795 --> 13:59.214
Well, let's meet again sometime
for another story.

13:59.839 --> 14:01.424
See you. Bye-bye.

14:01.508 --> 14:03.426
It's not "See you. Bye-bye"!

14:03.510 --> 14:05.804
Did you remember anything
about the logo or not?

14:05.887 --> 14:09.557
Oops. Maybe if I keep talking
it'll come back to me.

14:09.641 --> 14:11.643
I knew you'd say that!

14:11.726 --> 14:15.063
Cool it, Sis.
Let's just hear one more, at least.

14:15.146 --> 14:16.523
MENU - GREAT DISASTER
TRUE GHOST STORIES

14:16.606 --> 14:18.817
Tell us one of the true ghost stories.
"The Walled Town."

14:18.900 --> 14:20.276
Thank you.

14:20.777 --> 14:23.113
Then let's get back to it.

14:23.988 --> 14:26.616
This story is one of my own,
experienced firsthand.

14:26.700 --> 14:29.160
For ten years, from the age of 12,

14:29.786 --> 14:33.456
<i>I was shut up in a school</i>
<i>surrounded by walls.</i>

14:34.416 --> 14:37.877
I apologize for calling
an emergency meeting with everyone.

14:38.378 --> 14:42.382
Mina will send out meeting minutes
to the departments who cannot attend.

14:42.882 --> 14:46.803
First, in regards to the ongoing
search for an assistant director,

14:47.387 --> 14:49.806
I would like to ask Miss Aoshima
to take up the position.

14:55.311 --> 14:59.274
Miss Aoshima will be given
level-four access rights.

14:59.357 --> 15:00.734
Hold on one second.

15:01.317 --> 15:03.361
Why is Aoshima being promoted?

15:03.445 --> 15:07.574
Because Miss Aoshima
is the one I can trust the most.

15:11.578 --> 15:15.373
But Dr. Sawatari was supposed to be
the most likely future director.

15:15.874 --> 15:17.751
This is not going to go down well.

15:18.335 --> 15:19.836
Madame Takeuchi too.

15:21.796 --> 15:25.842
That town was a place where women ruled.

15:26.343 --> 15:30.930
There were around 30 women,
mostly between the ages of 20 and 40.

15:31.973 --> 15:35.435
<i>The school was their stronghold,</i>
<i>and they barricaded it in.</i>

15:35.935 --> 15:39.356
<i>Any man who accidentally approached it</i>
<i>would be killed.</i>

15:40.398 --> 15:42.233
<i>However, in rare cases,</i>

15:42.317 --> 15:44.694
<i>if they thought the man was healthy</i>
<i>and liked his face,</i>

15:45.195 --> 15:48.198
<i>they would imprison him in the town,</i>
<i>keeping him as a "breeding pig."</i>

15:49.115 --> 15:53.828
I spent ten years
in that town, as Boar #11.

15:54.662 --> 15:58.833
<i>The breeding pigs would perform tasks</i>
<i>and provide the women with sperm.</i>

15:59.793 --> 16:04.339
<i>When it was my turn,</i>
<i>one couple kept asking for me.</i>

16:05.173 --> 16:07.842
<i>Eventually, one of them fell pregnant.</i>

16:08.718 --> 16:12.347
<i>If a girl was born, she would be accepted</i>
<i>into the town as a human.</i>

16:12.931 --> 16:15.809
<i>But if it was a boy,</i>
<i>he would be taken from his mother</i>

16:15.892 --> 16:18.353
<i>and raised by us as a breeding pig.</i>

16:20.105 --> 16:22.649
<i>It was a boy.</i>

16:23.566 --> 16:27.570
<i>One night, about six months later,</i>
<i>that couple hatched a plan.</i>

16:27.654 --> 16:30.865
<i>The four of us</i>
<i>would flee the town together.</i>

16:30.949 --> 16:32.617
Yeah! Good for you!

16:33.702 --> 16:35.870
<i>But they found us…</i>

16:38.206 --> 16:40.709
<i>and only I barely managed to escape.</i>

16:43.294 --> 16:44.504
<i>The next day,</i>

16:44.587 --> 16:48.842
<i>the couple's slaughtered corpses</i>
<i>had been strung up outside the town walls.</i>

16:49.342 --> 16:51.469
<i>About one year has passed since then.</i>

16:52.470 --> 16:55.932
<i>That such a terrifying place</i>
<i>can even exist in this world, is…</i>

16:57.684 --> 16:59.936
So let's meet again sometime
for another story.

17:01.021 --> 17:02.564
See you. Bye-bye.

17:02.647 --> 17:04.566
It's not "See you. Bye bye"!

17:05.150 --> 17:06.693
What happened to the baby?

17:06.776 --> 17:07.819
I don't know.

17:07.902 --> 17:10.113
What a gruesome story.

17:10.613 --> 17:14.951
Sis, can't you go check somehow?
To see if the baby is at least alive?

17:15.035 --> 17:16.828
If the story is even true…

17:24.002 --> 17:26.880
I suppose you did tell us a story,
so I won't take the money back.

17:27.964 --> 17:29.924
But you better get lost before I kill you.

17:30.008 --> 17:31.885
I-I'm sorry!

17:32.469 --> 17:34.346
What was that for?

17:34.429 --> 17:35.889
He didn't tell us about the logo yet.

17:35.972 --> 17:37.432
He didn't need to.

17:37.515 --> 17:39.809
That guy was acting really strange.

17:40.393 --> 17:42.395
<i>Even though</i>
<i>the driver's seat is on the right,</i>

17:42.479 --> 17:44.647
<i>he went to the effort</i>
<i>to repark his car to the right.</i>

17:45.148 --> 17:46.149
In the first place,

17:47.108 --> 17:51.237
why park your car so close to the wall,
when there's no one around here?

17:53.740 --> 17:56.409
There was a reason
he needed to move it so quickly.

17:57.118 --> 17:59.245
He spotted something
that he wanted to hide.

18:00.246 --> 18:02.207
2F - TAKA

18:03.041 --> 18:05.126
TAKAHARA ACADEMY

18:05.210 --> 18:06.836
It's the logo on the Kiru-Beam.

18:07.420 --> 18:11.841
We nearly wasted all our time
and money on that endless storytelling.

18:13.593 --> 18:14.594
But we found it.

18:15.720 --> 18:17.097
The origin of the symbol.

18:20.433 --> 18:22.602
TAKAHARA ACADEMY

18:31.695 --> 18:33.154
That box!

18:34.864 --> 18:36.825
You found it.

18:36.908 --> 18:38.702
You really are an odd-job girl.

18:42.956 --> 18:45.542
We found the Kiru-Beam logo,

18:46.042 --> 18:49.129
but if this is heaven,
isn't it really just a normal building?

18:49.713 --> 18:51.214
Let's look around some more.

18:56.136 --> 18:59.472
Someone's already
scavenged through all this stuff.

19:13.236 --> 19:15.864
"Welcome message from the Director.

19:17.032 --> 19:21.578
At Takahara Academy, there is a space
where you can rest both body and mind.

19:22.370 --> 19:24.914
There is time
to immerse yourself in your hobbies,

19:25.498 --> 19:28.043
and people who will listen to you
in times of stress."

19:28.126 --> 19:29.127
HELL OF PATIENCE

19:30.045 --> 19:33.381
Just one more thing I don't understand
about life before the Great Disaster.

19:34.007 --> 19:37.886
Seems like an orphanage you can go to
even if you have a family and home…

19:37.969 --> 19:39.471
EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION
TAKAHARA ACADEMY

19:39.554 --> 19:41.431
…and it's also a cram school?

19:43.850 --> 19:47.937
The heaven-like civilization
of that period sounds like hard work.

19:51.983 --> 19:53.860
Well, maybe not all that bad.

19:54.486 --> 19:57.614
With a few friends,
maybe I'd have the patience for it.

20:00.533 --> 20:02.285
Sis! Will you come here?

20:03.620 --> 20:05.246
TAKAHARA ACADEMY

20:06.956 --> 20:09.250
Was this floor
part of Takahara Academy too?

20:11.961 --> 20:13.171
Over here.

20:17.634 --> 20:20.136
Another weird bird mark.

20:21.304 --> 20:24.474
But it just looks like someone
made a graffiti version of the other one.

20:24.974 --> 20:26.518
I bet bandits lived here at some point.

20:27.018 --> 20:28.395
I'm not sure how,

20:28.895 --> 20:31.731
but I get the feeling this place
isn't the one I've been searching for.

20:32.315 --> 20:33.942
And there's no one here who looks like me.

20:34.818 --> 20:38.863
I got all excited after we traced the logo
on the gun to this place,

20:40.031 --> 20:42.283
but there's also the possibility

20:42.367 --> 20:45.078
that the gun and the place I'm looking for
never had any connection.

20:47.330 --> 20:48.331
What's this?

20:48.415 --> 20:53.044
It seems that Takahara Academy
was some kind of orphanage.

20:53.837 --> 20:58.049
And in that guide, it describes the world
as a "Hell of Patience."

20:59.134 --> 21:00.969
And what's the opposite of hell, Maru?

21:01.720 --> 21:02.721
Heaven.

21:04.597 --> 21:06.933
So if the symbol
and this academy are related to heaven,

21:07.017 --> 21:09.352
I still think
it's worth following this lead.

21:09.436 --> 21:10.437
CONTACT NUMBERS

21:10.520 --> 21:11.604
According to the leaflet,

21:11.688 --> 21:14.441
Takahara Academy has two facilities
and 18 branches.

21:15.150 --> 21:18.069
I guess the other branches
could be similar to this one.

21:18.737 --> 21:20.739
I'm more curious about the two facilities.

21:21.906 --> 21:24.075
Ibaraki and Nara?

21:25.160 --> 21:27.787
It seems like an okay place to sleep.
Should we stay here tonight?

21:28.288 --> 21:30.832
No. Let's find somewhere else.

21:31.374 --> 21:33.043
This place gives me the shivers.

21:36.963 --> 21:39.007
Let's get onto the main topic.

21:40.050 --> 21:42.510
We have discovered that Tokio is pregnant.

21:43.845 --> 21:46.097
-What?
-B-B-But that's outrageous!

21:46.181 --> 21:47.849
At that young age!

21:47.932 --> 21:49.017
That's not the issue.

21:49.601 --> 21:51.269
The real question is the father!

21:51.353 --> 21:53.980
-Who is the father?
-Director?

21:54.064 --> 21:55.482
It's under investigation!

21:57.525 --> 22:00.028
We never taught them the concept of sex,

22:00.111 --> 22:02.113
or the distinction
between male and female.

22:02.197 --> 22:03.907
And now, in these crucial final moments…

22:05.784 --> 22:07.869
This could shake up
the entire Takahara Academy!

22:08.495 --> 22:10.455
<i>We are in a state of crisis!</i>
